{"key":"deadline-scheduling-9066971dde8d3051","sourceHash":"9066971dde8d3051077c5e517d50667244dd883441f9059331cbe98ad98888fb","pattern":"deadline-scheduling","category":"greedy-intervals","title":"Deadline Profit Scheduling: Mental Model","idea":"Process jobs by deadline while a heap keeps only the best feasible set.","complexity":"O(n log n) time · O(n) space","source":"fn maximum_profit(jobs: &[(usize, i32)]) -> i32 {\n    fn free(parent: &mut [usize], x: usize) -> usize {\n        if parent[x] != x {\n            parent[x] = free(parent, parent[x]);\n        }\n        parent[x]\n    }\n    let mut sorted = jobs.to_vec();\n    sorted.sort_by_key(|&(d, p)| (std::cmp::Reverse(p), d));\n    let n = jobs.len();\n    let mut parent: Vec<_> = (0..=n).collect();\n    let mut profit = 0;\n    for (deadline, value) in sorted {\n        if value <= 0 {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let slot = free(&mut parent, deadline.min(n));\n        if slot > 0 {\n            profit += value;\n            parent[slot] = free(&mut parent, slot - 1);\n        }\n    }\n    profit\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let result = maximum_profit(&[(2, 100), (1, 19), (2, 27), (1, 25), (3, 15)]).to_string();\n    println!(\"{result}\");\n}\n","sites":[{"line":8,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"let mut sorted = jobs.to_vec();"},{"line":9,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"sorted.sort_by_key(|&(d, p)| (std::cmp::Reverse(p), d));"},{"line":10,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"let n = jobs.len();"},{"line":11,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"let mut parent: Vec<_> = (0..=n).collect();"},{"line":12,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"let mut profit = 0;"},{"line":13,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"for (deadline, value) in sorted {"},{"line":14,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"if value <= 0 {"},{"line":15,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"continue;"},{"line":17,"function":"maximum_profit","statement":"let slot = free(&mut parent, deadline.mi